  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "has_data",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-kern-table.hh",
    "description": "OT::kern::has_data() performs an unconditional 32-bit read of u.version32 (`return u.version32 != 0;`) without first ensuring the `kern` table blob is at least 4 bytes. For this PoV, the font provides a truncated `kern` table (length 0x1a total table bytes in sfnt, with only 2 bytes of payload for kern), so accessing `u.version32` reads past the end of the allocated input buffer, causing a heap-buffer-overflow in BEInt<unsigned int,4>::operator unsigned int().",
    "conditions": "Data flow: hb-shape-fuzzer input is parsed as a font -> hb_shape_full() -> hb_ot_layout_has_kerning() -> _get_kern(face).has_data() -> OT::kern::has_data(). Trigger requires a font containing a `kern` table entry whose actual table data is shorter than 4 bytes (or otherwise truncated at end of file). Because has_data() is called before any size/sanitize guard for this specific read, the 4-byte version fetch overreads by 1+ bytes at buffer end."
  },
